  "decisions": [
    {
      "concept": "template_choice",
      "note": "Cross-checked against the pinned AFC NEMA-14 template templates/AFC_QuattroBox_14.cfg through the config/mcu/MMB_2.0_QB.cfg alias. AFC's filenames encode the motor, not a hardware revision -- include/install_functions.sh:123-145 selects AFC_QuattroBox_14.cfg for NEMA-14 geared motors (gear_ratio 50:10) and _17.cfg for NEMA-17 direct drive (1:1), and neither template's own header names a version. Happy Hare's QuattroBox v1.x declares a geared train (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.quattro_box PARAM_GEAR_GEAR_RATIO 50:17), so the geared NEMA-14 template is the match; v2.0 (PARAM_GEAR_GEAR_RATIO 1:1) pairs with _17. The rendered [mmu_stepper unit0_gear] shows gear_ratio 1:1 for every version -- the harness does not carry PARAM_GEAR_GEAR_RATIO into the trace -- so the geared/direct signal is the Kconfig header, not the rendered field."
    },
    {
      "concept": "arrival",
      "note": "Happy Hare's LOAD homes the bowden to the shared-exit switch (unit0:mmu_shared_exit, layout 10mm) and then runs the last bowden leg as a plain move -- one hub switch serves all four lanes, which is exactly the hub-sensor role klipper-mmu's has_hub_sensor/PINS_HUB covers. AFC's arrival concept is its [AFC_extruder] pin_tool_start ('enter_tool_pin', AFC_Hardware-QuattroBox.cfg), which is not part of the lane template, so the compare shows arrival as hh-only. Default: HH's shared-exit homing; the toolhead-entrance switch stays host wiring."
    },
    {
      "concept": "buffer_type",
      "note": "AFC configures a switched advance/trailing buffer by default (the Turtleneck its comment names: [AFC_buffer QuattroBox_1] advance_pin/trailing_pin, multiplier_high/low 1.05/0.95). Happy Hare's QuattroBox trace renders no [mmu_buffer] section at all, so the compare shows buffer_type as afc-only. klipper-mmu follows the extruder from a switched buffer like this one (`KLIPPER_MMU_PINS_BUFFER_A/B`), but does not use it for ramming arrival: LOAD ends at a local toolhead switch or at FPS arrival."
    },
    {
      "concept": "encoder",
      "note": "The QuattroBox family header selects MMU_HAS_ENCODER (installer/mmu_types/Kconfig.quattro_box), but the rendered unit0 hardware has no encoder node or pins -- the harness does not wire one. klipper-mmu's optional encoder input (`KLIPPER_MMU_ENCODER`) stays off by default for QuattroBox, and it has no encoder-homing mode."
    },
    {
      "concept": "espooler",
      "note": "QuattroBox is described as a Filamentalist respooler driven by the gear steppers (Kconfig.quattro_box help), but the trace renders no [mmu_espooler] section or assist pins. klipper-mmu's powered rewind (`KLIPPER_MMU_POWERED_REWIND`) is on by default only for BoxTurtle and Claymore; QuattroBox runs without espooler assist."
    },
    {
      "concept": "preload_park",
      "note": "Happy Hare parks PRELOAD 23mm behind the shared-exit switch (measured: tip -13 = shared exit 10 - 23; gate_preload_parking_distance -23). AFC's park_dist is 10mm. Default applied: HH's 23mm (the executable reference); AFC's 10mm recorded as the difference."
    },
    {
      "concept": "unload_park",
      "note": "Happy Hare parks UNLOAD 23mm behind the shared-exit switch as well (measured tip -13). AFC's hub_clear_move_dis is 65mm. Same direction, very different magnitude; default applied: HH's 23mm."
    },
    {
      "concept": "long_speed",
      "note": "AFC's global long_moves_speed/accel is 150/250 mm/s (config/AFC.cfg; the QuattroBox template sets no unit override). Happy Hare's gear_load_speed/accel is 100/100. Default applied: HH's 100/100."
    },
    {
      "concept": "short_speed",
      "note": "AFC's short_moves_speed/accel is 50/300; Happy Hare's gear_short_move_speed/accel is 80/400. Default applied: HH's 80/400 (the executable reference)."
    },
    {
      "concept": "bowden",
      "note": "AFC carries real lengths (afc_bowden_length 1145.0mm plus per-lane dist_hub 40-95mm in the NEMA-14 template); Happy Hare's dossier has no genuine bowden number (variable_bowden_lengths=0, require_bowden_move=1, autocal_bowden_length=0), so the compare row is afc-only. klipper-mmu's fps_calibrated_steps is one value per unit today, not per lane -- host-owned; gap recorded, not fabricated."
    }
  ]
}
